@startuml intro_programming_use_cases
' ============================================================
' Use Case Diagram — Intro to Programming (Python) Learning System
' Capstone A scope: core use cases only
' Agent decomposition follows the three-agent LCS model
' (Chan 1991): teacher agent, companion agent, student.
' Target user: student with no prior programming knowledge
' ============================================================

left to right direction
skinparam packageStyle rectangle
skinparam shadowing false
skinparam actorStyle awesome
skinparam usecase {
  BackgroundColor #FDFDFD
  BorderColor #666666
}

' ---------------- Actors ----------------
' Student, Companion and Teacher are the three agents of the LCS model.
' The student is a human actor; the other two are system agents.
actor "Student\n(no prior programming)" as Student
actor "Instructor" as Instructor
actor "Companion Agent" as Companion <<system>>
actor "Teacher Agent" as Teacher <<system>>
actor "Code Runner" as Runner <<system>>

' ---------------- System boundary ----------------
rectangle "Python Intro Programming Learning System" {

  usecase "UC1\nStart an exercise" as UC1
  usecase "UC2\nPlan the approach\nwith the companion" as UC2
  usecase "UC3\nDecide the plan" as UC3
  usecase "UC4\nWrite and run code" as UC4
  usecase "UC5\nView test results" as UC5
  usecase "UC6\nDiagnose a failure\ntogether" as UC6
  usecase "UC7\nRequest a hint" as UC7
  usecase "UC8\nView progress" as UC8
  usecase "UC9\nAuthor exercise\n+ test cases" as UC9
  usecase "UC10\nReceive teacher\nintervention" as UC10
}

' ---------------- Associations ----------------
Student --> UC1
Student --> UC2
Student --> UC3
Student --> UC4
Student --> UC5
Student --> UC7
Student --> UC8

Companion --> UC2
Companion --> UC6
Teacher --> UC10
Runner --> UC4

Instructor --> UC9
Instructor --> UC10

' ---------------- Relationships ----------------
UC2 ..> UC3 : <<include>>
UC3 ..> UC4 : <<include>>
UC4 ..> UC5 : <<include>>
UC5 ..> UC6 : <<extend>>
UC4 ..> UC7 : <<extend>>
UC6 ..> UC10 : <<extend>>
UC7 ..> UC10 : <<extend>>

' ---------------- Notes ----------------
note right of UC3
  The student makes the final call.
  The companion may disagree,
  but never overrides.
end note

note bottom of UC4
  The companion implements the
  student's chosen plan **even when
  it is wrong**, so the error surfaces
  by running the code rather than
  by being told.
end note

note right of UC10
  The teacher agent holds the complete,
  correct rule set; the companion sees a
  restricted view of the same knowledge
  base. It intervenes only after N failed
  rounds or on explicit student request,
  so student and companion still converge
  on the learning goals.
end note

@enduml
